# =============================================================================
# Dockerfile-specific production build context rules.
#
# Patterns are relative to the repo-root context, not this file. Builds use COPY . . to ingest
# the full Nx monorepo, so only exclude items that the build doesn't need.
# =============================================================================

# -- Version control ----------------------------------------------------------
# The root `.gitignore` stays: Nx hashes it (with `nx.json`) into every task, and builds by it which
# files exist, so without it no task hashed here matched a CI cache entry (CI audit 2026-11-12, F5)
# and the API targets, run after their dependencies, also hashed those dependencies' `dist` output.
.git
.gitattributes

# -- External dependency repos (86 GB locally, gitignored but not dockerignored) --
repos

# -- Generated reports and artifacts ------------------------------------------
/out

# -- E2E test projects (not needed in the API production image) ---------------
apps/ui-e2e
apps/api-e2e
# The root tsconfig.json references both. `@oxc-node/core` drops the whole tsconfig when a
# reference is missing and falls back to a target without top-level await, so a build script
# such as `cli:stage-acp` fails to load. Each solution file has no sources and adds no project.
!apps/ui-e2e/tsconfig.json
!apps/api-e2e/tsconfig.json

# -- Documentation (not needed at build time) ---------------------------------
docs

# -- CI / tooling / editor config ---------------------------------------------
# `scripts` stays in the context: it is an Nx project that `runtime-e2e` lists
# as an implicit dependency, and the project graph fails without it.
.github
# `build-image.mts` runs every Nx call through CI's Nx guard and remote cache relay.
!.github/actions/setup-nx/nx-guard.ts
.claude/worktrees
.cursor
.vscode
.idea
.editorconfig
.eslintcache
.oxlintcache
.prettierrc*
.lintstagedrc*
tools/git-hooks

# -- Nx caches and workspace data --------------------------------------------
**/.nx/cache
**/.nx/workspace-data

# -- Build artifacts (produced locally, not needed in fresh Docker build) ------
**/build
**/dist
**/out-tsc
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# -- Dependencies (installed fresh inside Docker) -----------------------------
**/node_modules

# -- Environment variables (secrets, never ship) ------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
# The tracked placeholder templates are inputs of `api:build` on CI, so the image hashes them too.
# They hold no values, and only the build stage sees them: the runtime images copy `pnpm deploy`
# output, which is each package's `files`.
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.test

# -- Test files stay in the context ------------------------------------------
# Nx infers each project's npm dependencies from every source file, tests included, and hashes
# them into the project's tasks, so a context without tests hashed a different graph than CI. The
# runtime images never see them: they copy only `pnpm deploy` output.
# -- Vite timestamp files ----------------------------------------------------
**/vite.config.*.timestamp*

# -- Fly.io config (injected via --config flag, not COPY) ---------------------
fly.*.toml

# -- Miscellaneous ------------------------------------------------------------
**/.cache
**/pruned
**/.next
**/.netlify
**/stats.html
*.md
LICENSE
CODEOWNERS
docker-compose.yml
infra
# The API image seeds the public bucket's two default images at boot (`apps/api/vite.config.ts` copies them).
!infra/seed

# Package builds copy this generated inventory into published distributions.
!docs/licensing/third-party-licenses.md
